From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 02:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] wanderer: tell the boot splash when the desktop has icons

m68k-emu68 keeps its boot splash on the framebuffer past the point where the
display driver would normally take it, so that the boot does not end on several
seconds of empty Workbench. Deciding when to let go needs to know when the
icons exist, and nothing in the system was in a position to say so.

Looked for a signal before settling for a heuristic, and there is none.
IconList has no attribute or notification meaning "the read finished". The
Startup-Sequence cannot help: it blocks on WANDERER:Wanderer, so a line after
it runs when Wanderer exits. MUIM_IconWindow_Open is the moment the backdrop
window opens, which is exactly the too-early moment the hold exists to get past.

So the signal is added where the knowledge already is. IconVolumeList's Update
is what fills the backdrop window, and a Bellatrix desktop opens on volumes --
RAM Disk and the boot volume. Sent once, after the super method has taken the
new entries, through bootui.resource.

It is a hint, not a command, and the splash treats it as one. "The icons are in
the list" is not "the icons are painted" -- MUI lays out on this message and
draws on the next redraw -- so the signal only arms the release, and the splash
still waits for the drawing to settle before letting go. A Wanderer that never
sends it costs a slower hand-off on a deadline and nothing else, which is why
this is guarded and unconditional rather than wired into anything.
---
--- a/workbench/system/Wanderer/Classes/iconvolumelist.c
+++ b/workbench/system/Wanderer/Classes/iconvolumelist.c
@@ -5,6 +5,26 @@
 #define DEBUG 0
 #include <aros/debug.h>
 
+#ifdef __EMU68__
+/*
+ * Telling the boot splash that the desktop has something on it.
+ *
+ * m68k-emu68 keeps its splash on the framebuffer past the point where the
+ * display driver would normally take it, so that the boot does not end on
+ * several seconds of empty Workbench. Deciding when to let go needs to know
+ * when the icons exist, and nothing else in the system is in a position to
+ * say: the Startup-Sequence blocks on WANDERER:Wanderer, and IconList has no
+ * attribute or notification meaning "the read finished".
+ *
+ * This is the place that does know. Sent once, from the volume list that fills
+ * the backdrop window -- the icons a Bellatrix desktop opens with are volumes.
+ * It is a hint and not a command: the splash still waits for the drawing to
+ * settle after this, and gives up on a deadline if it never arrives, so a
+ * Wanderer that never sends it costs a slower hand-off and nothing else.
+ */
+#include <aros/bootui.h>
+#endif
+
 #include <proto/exec.h>
 #include <proto/graphics.h>
 #include <proto/utility.h>
@@ -834,6 +854,24 @@
 
     DoSuperMethodA(CLASS, obj, (Msg) message);
 
+#ifdef __EMU68__
+    {
+        /* Once. Update runs again whenever a volume appears or goes away, and
+         * the splash is long gone by then. */
+        static BOOL bootui_told = FALSE;
+
+        if (!bootui_told)
+        {
+            struct BootUIResource *bootui =
+                (struct BootUIResource *)OpenResource(BOOTUI_RESOURCE_NAME);
+
+            bootui_told = TRUE;
+            if (bootui && bootui->set_stage)
+                bootui->set_stage(BOOTUI_STAGE_ICONS);
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     return 1;
 }
 
